  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 132 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nSoutherly return flow and clear skies allow for tempertures to rise \ninto the 60s for most on Sunday. A warming trend continues through \nthe end next week as Gulf moisture moves back into our area. Chances \nof rain (10-40%) return by midweek from the west due to upslope \nflow and embedded shortwaves moving through southwest flow aloft. \nBy the latter half of the week, guidance shows more widespread \nchances of rain as an upper trough approaches the region and \npotentially increasing large-scale forcing for ascent. However, \nthere is much uncertainty in rain coverage and amounts at this \ntime. This will depend on the track of the trough and moisture \nquality. Naturally, we will continue to monitor trends and details\nshall become more clear in the coming days.\n  \nGreening",
